# Software engineering

## Traceability

- Contract: single source `src/lib/report-schema.ts` (keep in sync with `docs/MVP.md` §5). MVP cites MVP sections; V2+ cites `RNCK-REQ-nnn` in `docs/requirements/MRL.md`.
- AI-generated code must be verifiable (tests or typed boundaries).
- After substantive edits: agent runs `pnpm test` and `pnpm lint` (and `pnpm build` when relevant) before handing off — see `agent-execution` rule.

## Dependencies

- Lockfile committed. New npm package: state **pain point** and why platform/ existing code is insufficient (in PR/chat).
- Prefer Vercel, Supabase, and `ai` SDK over custom HTTP stacks.

## Abstraction (YAGNI)

- Extract module/helper only after **3rd repetition** or a **V2/MVP-documented** need — not for hypothetical futures.
- MVP tests only: **report schema**, **phone normalize**, **search handler** unit tests. No E2E framework in MVP.

## Data and migrations

- Synthetic test data only. Migrations reversible or document rollback in the same change.

## Phase V2+

- SBOM, dependency audit, immutable deploy hashes — enable per `docs/phases/V2-roadmap.md`, not before.
